+type: comment
+---
+
+Already-applied requirement updates already omitted `conflicts`; the real gap was a stale patch the store would refuse (bad title/text), which also came back with no conflicts and read as "already applied" — it now names every field it carries.
+Table tests cover already-applied, partial overlap and real conflict in the vault, MCP `update_requirement` and HTTP PATCH.
+The web requirement detail treats a `stale_revision` with no conflicts as "Already saved" (block edits and status moves): it reloads, with no alert or error; docs/05, 07, 08 and CHANGELOG updated.
